1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,269
This is PressPath TV, a family app for Android TV that measures navigation inside its own interface.

2
00:00:06,519 --> 00:00:12,447
Everything you see is the real release APK on an Android TV emulator, controlled only with D-pad presses.

3
00:00:13,447 --> 00:00:18,535
Home offers the Navigation Lab, Memory Pairs, Flashcards, Progress and Settings.

4
00:00:18,785 --> 00:00:22,170
The evidence card is empty, because nothing has been measured yet.

5
00:00:23,170 --> 00:00:29,320
The Navigation Lab runs five guided tasks and records real presses, backtracks, edge misses and seconds.

6
00:00:29,570 --> 00:00:33,051
Task two: open Science flashcards and reveal an answer.

7
00:00:33,051 --> 00:00:35,076
The live bar counts every press.

8
00:00:36,070 --> 00:00:38,893
7 presses, saved as baseline run 1.

9
00:00:40,093 --> 00:00:42,315
A second baseline run of the same task.

10
00:00:48,093 --> 00:00:49,177
7 presses.

11
00:00:50,677 --> 00:00:55,465
Rule R1 fires when a task needs five or more presses in at least two baseline runs.

12
00:00:55,715 --> 00:00:58,901
The preview cites both runs before anything changes.

13
00:00:58,901 --> 00:01:00,556
The tiles keep their order.

14
00:01:00,556 --> 00:01:02,394
Only a Home shortcut is added.

15
00:01:05,777 --> 00:01:06,345
Apply.

16
00:01:08,645 --> 00:01:12,580
Now the adaptive run: up to the new shortcut, OK, and reveal.

17
00:01:13,645 --> 00:01:14,647
3 presses.

18
00:01:15,847 --> 00:01:17,854
Next, open Before and After.

19
00:01:19,947 --> 00:01:23,946
It compares the medians of the recorded runs: 7 presses down to 3.

20
00:01:24,947 --> 00:01:29,255
That is −4, or −57%, measured on this device.

21
00:01:30,455 --> 00:01:31,936
Every change is reversible.

22
00:01:32,455 --> 00:01:35,684
Undo removes the shortcut, and the recorded runs are kept.

23
00:01:39,891 --> 00:01:45,679
Memory Pairs is fully playable with the remote: 12 cards and 6 pairs, with pairs found and moves.

24
00:01:45,991 --> 00:01:47,698
There is no timer and no score.

25
00:01:50,398 --> 00:01:53,706
Flashcards cover Letters, Numbers and Everyday Science.

26
00:01:53,956 --> 00:01:57,184
OK reveals the answer, and Next moves to the next card.

27
00:01:58,284 --> 00:02:00,247
Back returns focus to where you were.

28
00:02:03,884 --> 00:02:07,978
Settings provides High Contrast, with a yellow focus ring on pure black.

29
00:02:08,284 --> 00:02:13,417
Large Text enlarges the interface text, and Reduce Motion turns off zoom and transitions.

30
00:02:17,284 --> 00:02:22,516
Clear All Local Data always asks for confirmation first, so nothing is deleted by accident.

31
00:02:23,716 --> 00:02:29,149
PressPath TV works offline, requests no permissions, and keeps its data on the device.

32
00:02:29,399 --> 00:02:32,086
It was verified on an Android TV emulator.

33
00:02:32,086 --> 00:02:34,837
It has not been tested on Fire TV hardware.

34
00:02:35,087 --> 00:02:36,438
Every press counts.

35
00:02:36,438 --> 00:02:38,144
Every path gets smarter.
